course: dictionary
lesson: 3747
title: Fluent and fluency
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Fluent» describes something done smoothly and easily. A fluent reader reads without stopping at every word, and a fluent speaker can use a language easily and well. The word can be an adjective («a fluent reader»), an adverb («fluently») or a noun («fluency»).
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Fluent readers still use phonics, fast and silently, and slow down to it when they meet a hard new word.» Fluent readers are quick and smooth, but they still slow down for a hard word. So fluent does not mean never stopping. It means reading easily most of the time.
explain: «Chatbots... write fluent answers that can be helpful and also wrong.» Here fluent means smooth and easy to read, even when the answer is not true. A text can sound fluent and still be wrong, so check the meaning, not just how smooth it sounds.
fact: Fluent means able to do something easily and well, without stopping or struggling.
fact: «Fluent» can describe a language: «fluent in French» means you can speak it easily and well.
fact: «Fluent» can also describe smooth, graceful movement, as in «fluent movements».
fact: «Fluency» is the noun. In maths it means knowing facts, such as times tables, quickly and accurately.
fact: Smooth is not always the same as correct. Always check a fluent answer.
exercise: «Fluent readers still use phonics, fast and silently, and slow down when they meet a hard new word.» What does fluent mean in this sentence? | Loud and angry | *Able to read smoothly and easily | Asleep in bed | Reading very slowly, one word at a time
exercise: Maya says she is fluent in Spanish. What does that mean? | She knows only one Spanish word | She has never heard any Spanish | *She can speak Spanish easily and well | She wrote a book about Spain
exercise: What does fluent mean in «The dancer's movements were fluent and graceful»? | Tired and sore | Fast and loud | Hidden behind the stage | *Smooth and graceful
test: In maths, what does fluency mean? | Drawing a very neat graph | *Knowing facts like times tables quickly and accurately | Writing very long sums | Counting on your fingers only
test: «Chatbots write fluent answers that can be helpful and also wrong.» What does this teach us? | *A smooth answer can still be wrong | Fluent answers are always short | A smooth answer is always true | Chatbots never write answers
exam: Which word fits the gap? «Priya read the poem ___, with no stumbles.» | fluency | fluent | *fluently | fluents
